## 3. Data Structures

### Recommended Visuals
- Arrays
- Linked lists
- Stacks and queues
- Trees
- Graphs

### Search Keywords
- `data structures array linked list diagram`
- `stack and queue visualization`
- `tree and graph data structures diagram`

### Source
- [OpenDSA](https://opendsa-server.cs.vt.edu/)

### Visual Requirements
- Clearly label each data structure.
- Show connections between nodes where relevant.
- Avoid overcrowding the diagram.

**Suggested Caption:**

> Data structures organize information to make storing, accessing, and processing data more efficient.

---

## 4. Connectionist AI

### Recommended Visuals
- Artificial neural network
- Input, hidden, and output layers
- Nodes and weighted connections
- Neural network learning process

### Search Keywords
- `artificial neural network input hidden output layers diagram`
- `neural network nodes weights educational illustration`
- `neural network training process diagram`

### Source
- [Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org/)

### Visual Requirements
- Label the input, hidden, and output layers.
- Use nodes to represent artificial neurons.
- Use connecting lines to represent weighted connections.
- Prefer educational diagrams over generic robot illustrations.

**Suggested Caption:**

> Connectionist AI uses networks of interconnected computational units to learn patterns from data and generate predictions or decisions.

